WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:03.661
There are 12 of them.

00:00:04.881 --> 00:00:07.602
12 stadiums built in the four corners of Europe.

00:00:10.962 --> 00:00:16.243
Conceived by the most daring architects and built by thousands of workers and engineers.

00:00:20.245 --> 00:00:25.126
12 gigantic arenas selected to host matches for a global event,

00:00:25.507 --> 00:00:27.466
the 2020 European Football Championship.

00:00:31.555 --> 00:00:36.582
...embark on a unique tour of Europe to discover the most beautiful stadiums on the continent.

00:01:02.299 --> 00:01:03.119
In this episode,

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:09.822
The match will pit the Olympic Stadium in Rome, Italy against the San Mames Stadium in Bilbao, Spain.

00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:29.135
On one hand,

00:01:29.596 --> 00:01:30.577
a historic stadium.

00:01:31.198 --> 00:01:33.941
A stadium built in barely two years and which,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.703
to meet construction deadlines,

00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:38.325
demanded revolutionary technologies.

00:01:40.246 --> 00:01:40.768
For FIFA,

00:01:40.887 --> 00:01:43.870
It was impossible to build this stadium in such a short time.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.032
It was a true miracle.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:51.500
On the other hand,

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.822
a stadium fully integrated into the city which has successfully met a major challenge.

00:01:56.343 --> 00:02:00.646
To preserve the mythical atmosphere of the old San Mames stadium while modernizing it.

00:02:01.186 --> 00:02:04.328
The atmosphere in the stadium is deafening.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:08.012
The players feel it and it makes their hair stand on end.

00:02:12.354 --> 00:02:17.639
Two stadiums that took the gamble of destroying everything in order to rebuild everything in record time.

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:39.471
Let's begin

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:42.091
our journey through Italy and its eternal city,

00:02:42.431 --> 00:02:42.752
Rome.

00:02:44.679 --> 00:02:46.540
Located in the west-central part of the peninsula,

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.221
crossed by the Tiber,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.582
The Mediterranean capital is home to 3 million inhabitants.

00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:56.204
A veritable open-air history book,

00:02:56.765 --> 00:02:58.765
Rome oscillates between tradition and modernity.

00:03:01.187 --> 00:03:05.149
Exceptional historical monuments stand alongside contemporary architectural works,

00:03:08.131 --> 00:03:09.790
like the Foro Italico.

00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:15.686
Built under Mussolini between 1927 and 1933,

00:03:16.727 --> 00:03:22.250
This large sports complex houses remarkable remains adjacent to a large modern building.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:23.811
the Olympic stadium.

00:03:32.675 --> 00:03:34.676
Through this vast architectural complex,

00:03:35.436 --> 00:03:39.560
The Italian despot wished to consolidate his power and promote his regime.

00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:43.448
To reach the stadium,

00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:46.812
You have to take a central artery 130 meters long.

00:03:47.652 --> 00:03:48.293
Upon entering,

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:50.495
a gigantic marble obelisk,

00:03:50.895 --> 00:03:53.717
37 meters high and weighing over 300 tons.

00:03:58.062 --> 00:04:01.365
The Mussolini obelisk still sparks much controversy.

00:04:01.984 --> 00:04:05.228
because the Mussolini-Dux inscription is still present.

00:04:07.409 --> 00:04:09.271
The arrival of this monolith was epic.

00:04:10.591 --> 00:04:20.194
It was transported by river on a barge before being carried in front of St. Peter's Basilica as if to pay homage to the Pope.

00:04:22.034 --> 00:04:25.735
Then it was left on the ground on the central artery for several years.

00:04:26.057 --> 00:04:28.877
In 1932,

00:04:28.916 --> 00:04:29.918
the two architects,

00:04:29.997 --> 00:04:31.798
Constantini and Piantonello,

00:04:33.678 --> 00:04:37.240
have modified the base of the monolith, reminiscent of avant-garde architecture.

00:04:41.021 --> 00:04:43.802
To install the monolith in its final position,

00:04:45.444 --> 00:04:51.067
They used a lever system that allowed them to tilt the obelisk vertically.

00:04:53.929 --> 00:04:55.069
On this central artery,

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.572
The floor is decorated with 5000 m2 of mosaic that celebrates sport.

00:05:02.699 --> 00:05:05.821
22 marble blocks were erected on either side of the walkway.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:11.423
The Italico forum,

00:05:12.004 --> 00:05:14.285
designed by architect Enrico del Debbio,

00:05:14.845 --> 00:05:17.225
is centered around the spherical fountain square.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:26.430
It is from this fountain that the paths leading to the various sports facilities begin.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:28.629
The Olympic stadium,

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.571
formerly known as the Cypress Stadium,

00:05:31.312 --> 00:05:32.172
tennis courts,

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.381
The rugby pitch,

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:34.701
swimming pools,

00:05:35.302 --> 00:05:36.742
basketball or volleyball courts,

00:05:37.624 --> 00:05:44.530
the central walkway of the complex which runs through the Fascist male academy of physical education and Mussolini's private gymnasium.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.171
Finally, to conclude,

00:05:46.671 --> 00:05:47.672
the marble stadium,

00:05:47.953 --> 00:05:50.735
dominated by 62 monumental statues of athletes.

00:05:55.859 --> 00:06:01.744
The sculpted crown is the result of a competition in which artists from all over the country participated.

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:05.491
Each statue was paid for by a different municipality in Italy.

00:06:11.577 --> 00:06:15.520
The Foro Italico is designed to host major international competitions.

00:06:16.101 --> 00:06:16.922
And from the very beginning,

00:06:17.462 --> 00:06:20.045
special attention is given to the Cypress Stadium.

00:06:21.786 --> 00:06:27.812
It was built in 1927 by the architect Del Debbio and is located on the current site of the Olympic Stadium.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.061
In 1937,

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:35.461
another architect,

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:36.482
Luigi Moretti,

00:06:37.162 --> 00:06:40.103
resumes the project and adds two rings to the Cyprès stadium.

00:06:41.723 --> 00:06:42.984
Although still under construction,

00:06:43.705 --> 00:06:46.946
The enclosure has the makings of a monument worthy of being displayed to the world.

00:06:48.026 --> 00:06:52.008
Mussolini's regime chose it to host Hitler's visit in 1938.

00:06:53.569 --> 00:06:54.149
For the occasion,

00:06:54.929 --> 00:06:58.451
The stadium is decorated with 24 towers topped with imperial eagles,

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:00.672
immediately dismantled after the event.

00:07:08.012 --> 00:07:10.895
Construction of the stadium was then interrupted by the Second World War.

00:07:13.617 --> 00:07:25.807
then resumed in 1950 to give rise to the stadium of one hundred thousand.

00:07:25.809 --> 00:07:29.551
It was called the stadium of one hundred thousand because there were one hundred thousand spectators.

00:07:31.213 --> 00:07:34.035
It was huge and many people were standing.

00:07:35.117 --> 00:07:37.319
Major events have taken place in this stadium.

00:07:40.382 --> 00:07:40.963
Regularly,

00:07:41.605 --> 00:07:43.968
The 100,000 stadium is in the spotlight.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.172
In 1960,

00:07:47.732 --> 00:07:49.093
It hosts the Olympic Games,

00:07:49.533 --> 00:07:51.036
then the European football championships,

00:07:51.677 --> 00:07:53.559
but also the World Athletics Championships.

00:08:00.324 --> 00:08:01.964
From 1987 onwards,

00:08:02.766 --> 00:08:06.187
A major construction project will completely alter the morphology of the stadium.

00:08:16.651 --> 00:08:18.093
In May 1990,

00:08:18.793 --> 00:08:27.437
The new Olympic stadium was inaugurated and blessed by Pope John Paul II before hosting the first World Cup match between Italy and Austria.

00:08:35.399 --> 00:08:35.779
Today,

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:41.302
The second largest sports venue in the country is home to both clubs of the capital,

00:08:41.883 --> 00:08:44.264
AS Roma and Lazio of Rome.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:56.441
If in Rome,

00:08:56.701 --> 00:09:00.303
The venue is located away from the city centre in a large sports complex.

00:09:04.567 --> 00:09:05.168
in Bilbao,

00:09:05.969 --> 00:09:10.293
Sadmames Stadium has always been located in the very heart of the Basque city.

00:09:10.874 --> 00:09:12.394
bordered by small mountains.

00:09:22.015 --> 00:09:26.938
The first stadium, nicknamed the cathedral of football, was built in 1913.

00:09:30.639 --> 00:09:31.880
From the 1950s onwards,

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.902
It gradually expanded by adding stands all around it.

00:09:45.847 --> 00:09:51.032
The stadium will be completely transformed in just two years of work and inaugurated in 2013.

00:09:52.072 --> 00:09:54.254
It is located in the same place as the previous one.

00:09:55.816 --> 00:09:58.177
Because for the fervent supporters of Athletic Bilbao,

00:09:59.058 --> 00:09:59.980
It was unthinkable not to do it.

00:10:00.019 --> 00:10:01.881
to move the new stadium to the outskirts.

00:10:03.302 --> 00:10:04.504
This veritable institution,

00:10:04.923 --> 00:10:06.686
ambassador of a territory and a people,

00:10:07.245 --> 00:10:08.687
had to stay in the city centre.

00:10:14.393 --> 00:10:15.573
This is Caesar Ascarate,

00:10:16.053 --> 00:10:17.034
Spanish architect,

00:10:17.475 --> 00:10:19.557
who was tasked with designing the new stadium.

00:10:23.059 --> 00:10:27.344
The tradition of fans coming to this place for over 120 years,

00:10:27.836 --> 00:10:28.896
We couldn't change it.

00:10:30.717 --> 00:10:34.278
And to find other alternatives for moving the stadium out of the city,

00:10:34.639 --> 00:10:36.960
The club itself and the supporters prevented it.

00:10:42.961 --> 00:10:43.983
Located along the river,

00:10:44.182 --> 00:10:44.603
the Ria,

00:10:45.302 --> 00:10:48.024
The stadium is a key architectural element of the city.

00:10:53.527 --> 00:10:56.108
It follows in the tradition of landmark monuments.

00:10:57.228 --> 00:10:59.171
The town hall dates from the 19th century,

00:11:00.152 --> 00:11:03.897
the Guggenheim Museum, built in 1997 by Frank Gehry,

00:11:04.839 --> 00:11:07.182
the Euskalduna Congress and Music Palace,

00:11:09.185 --> 00:11:13.350
and the Iberdrola tower, covered in glass and 165 meters high.

00:11:29.792 --> 00:11:33.352
The most renowned architects participated in the transformation of Bilbao.

00:11:34.553 --> 00:11:40.075
This former industrial city has reinvented itself to become one of the most attractive cities in Spain.

00:11:43.616 --> 00:11:44.856
Located in the heart of the city,

00:11:45.476 --> 00:11:48.937
The site is easily accessible and served by public transport.

00:11:50.298 --> 00:11:50.839
Pedestrians,

00:11:51.019 --> 00:11:51.139
them,

00:11:51.678 --> 00:11:53.519
they take Licencia de Oposa street.

00:11:56.288 --> 00:11:59.211
The stadium is in a very important location in the city.

00:11:59.812 --> 00:12:01.875
right in front of Licenciado Posa street.

00:12:02.775 --> 00:12:05.018
This classic and legendary street in Bilbao,

00:12:05.899 --> 00:12:08.922
because from there you have an unobstructed view of the stadium.

00:12:09.501 --> 00:12:12.164
And this is where the fans arrive on match days.

00:12:12.826 --> 00:12:15.989
It's almost like a pilgrimage to the football stadium.

00:12:19.336 --> 00:12:25.239
This passionate man had to be brimming with inventiveness to integrate the arena as seamlessly as possible into the urban landscape.

00:12:26.639 --> 00:12:29.822
He then divided the facade into five rings of identical height.

00:12:30.402 --> 00:12:32.864
similar to the floors of a typical downtown building.

00:12:34.585 --> 00:12:37.505
He then decorated it with patterns resembling boat sails.

00:12:44.049 --> 00:12:48.451
This shape is repeated 2500 times and we have distributed it over 5 floors.

00:12:49.552 --> 00:12:50.313
In this way,

00:12:50.913 --> 00:12:55.737
This allows for a building on a human scale and in harmony with the other buildings in the city.

00:12:59.018 --> 00:13:00.619
But with its 55,000 seats,

00:13:01.119 --> 00:13:04.860
The new stadium also had to meet the challenge of being larger,

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:07.640
taller and more impressive than the old one,

00:13:08.241 --> 00:13:10.261
without encroaching further on the city.

00:13:13.342 --> 00:13:14.063
As you can see,

00:13:14.403 --> 00:13:16.024
He is quite well integrated into the city.

00:13:16.364 --> 00:13:18.485
both in height and size.

00:13:20.605 --> 00:13:21.025
You know,

00:13:21.405 --> 00:13:25.927
Football stadiums are generally the largest monuments in cities in terms of size and volume.

00:13:29.109 --> 00:13:35.672
We therefore had to reduce its footprint so that it occupies as little space as possible and reduce its height to the maximum.

00:13:38.633 --> 00:13:40.914
So that it is at the same level as the city's buildings.

00:13:44.855 --> 00:13:45.756
To achieve this,

00:13:46.556 --> 00:13:52.218
We had the ground buried approximately 8 meters below street level, which reduced the height of the stadium.

00:13:56.119 --> 00:13:59.781
The new Sad Mames stadium is one of the most compact stadiums in the world.

00:14:01.262 --> 00:14:04.223
If the architect has succeeded in integrating the structure into the urban fabric,

00:14:04.924 --> 00:14:07.505
The manufacturers still faced a double challenge.

00:14:12.068 --> 00:14:17.250
How to go from a stadium with a capacity of 43,000 to 53,000 spectators while staying in the same location?

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:22.600
But also how to build the new structure,

00:14:23.381 --> 00:14:24.923
before even destroying the old one,

00:14:27.844 --> 00:14:30.186
and while the team continues to play its home games.

00:14:44.653 --> 00:14:47.515
The challenge was to successfully build the wall between the river and the river.

00:14:48.396 --> 00:14:49.177
The old stadium,

00:14:49.599 --> 00:14:51.883
a hotel and the city's university.

00:14:55.551 --> 00:14:56.132
Oscar Malot,

00:14:56.353 --> 00:14:57.715
today, stadium director

00:14:58.115 --> 00:15:00.000
followed the project at the time as an engineer.

00:15:07.785 --> 00:15:11.528
The construction of the stadium was very tightly controlled because the plot of land is very small.

00:15:13.529 --> 00:15:14.029
And above all,

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:18.072
The old stadium was to continue operating while the new one was being built.

00:15:21.034 --> 00:15:27.499
The maneuvers of each element and each machine that we used during construction were very limited.

00:15:30.091 --> 00:15:37.038
And the challenge is all the greater because this future football temple must be built while respecting the neighborhood located just a few meters away.

00:15:41.629 --> 00:15:42.689
Since the stadium is in the city,

00:15:42.909 --> 00:15:44.870
We needed to limit our noise pollution.

00:15:46.591 --> 00:15:47.793
We have a hotel next door.

00:15:47.992 --> 00:15:49.312
relatively close neighbors.

00:15:50.573 --> 00:15:51.054
So at night,

00:15:51.095 --> 00:15:51.495
Of course,

00:15:51.534 --> 00:15:55.057
It was necessary to prioritize the least noisy tasks so that the neighbors could sleep.

00:15:56.418 --> 00:15:56.758
So yes,

00:15:56.817 --> 00:16:01.280
This limited our room for maneuver and we really had to intensify the work during the daytime hours.

00:16:07.511 --> 00:16:08.032
In total,

00:16:08.692 --> 00:16:10.073
That's more than 15 machines.

00:16:10.333 --> 00:16:10.914
4 cranes,

00:16:11.274 --> 00:16:13.496
some of which reach 150 meters in height,

00:16:13.996 --> 00:16:18.880
who worked on the site for months and removed more than 33,000 tons of rubble.

00:16:21.282 --> 00:16:24.365
A colossal construction project in the heart of the city.

00:16:32.887 --> 00:16:34.208
The dimensions of the new stadium,

00:16:34.328 --> 00:16:35.608
designed by the architects,

00:16:36.168 --> 00:16:39.691
were 236 meters long by 191 meters wide.

00:16:41.072 --> 00:16:45.953
But the space between the riverside roads and the old stadium was only 156 meters.

00:16:48.034 --> 00:16:49.254
From May 2010,

00:16:49.915 --> 00:16:53.256
Only the first three-quarters of the stadium were built on the available space.

00:16:53.996 --> 00:16:55.197
without touching the old stadium,

00:16:55.677 --> 00:16:57.438
which continued to host the club's matches.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:00.921
During the summer of 2013,

00:17:01.721 --> 00:17:03.121
The old stadium has been demolished.

00:17:06.565 --> 00:17:09.026
The deadline was 22 months for the first stage.

00:17:09.346 --> 00:17:11.127
That's a very short time for building a stadium.

00:17:13.449 --> 00:17:17.511
And the biggest challenge was demolishing the street that separated the old stadium from the new one.

00:17:20.513 --> 00:17:20.713
Of course,

00:17:20.733 --> 00:17:22.074
the stands of the old stadium,

00:17:22.434 --> 00:17:24.715
whose arch was the emblem of the old Saint-Mames.

00:17:27.596 --> 00:17:28.156
At that moment,

00:17:28.216 --> 00:17:36.500
We only had three months to do this demolition and gain the 10 meters of turf that the new stadium needed to reach the regulation dimensions.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:40.721
That's where things got tricky.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.481
because if we don't meet the deadlines,

00:17:42.621 --> 00:17:44.862
We ended up without the old stadium and without the new one.

00:17:48.503 --> 00:17:49.724
After the lawn was laid out,

00:17:50.424 --> 00:17:54.807
The last quarter of the stands was able to be built during the 2013-2014 season.

00:17:55.267 --> 00:17:57.728
while the club was playing its matches in its new stadium,

00:17:58.367 --> 00:17:59.209
still under construction.

00:18:04.631 --> 00:18:08.113
While the construction of the San Mames stadium was a race against time,

00:18:08.593 --> 00:18:11.274
The same is true for another legendary football venue,

00:18:12.894 --> 00:18:14.174
the Olympic Stadium in Rome.

00:18:28.466 --> 00:18:34.110
To host the 1990 FIFA World Cup and meet the standards of international organizations,

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:37.212
The stadium in the Italian capital must be destroyed.

00:18:38.293 --> 00:18:41.115
then rebuilt in barely two years.

00:18:42.312 --> 00:18:43.254
A record time.

00:18:46.759 --> 00:18:49.742
When the FIFA representatives came to see the progress of the work,

00:18:51.225 --> 00:18:52.908
They wanted to take the World Cup away from us.

00:18:53.889 --> 00:18:57.775
because they said it was impossible to build the stadium in such a short time.

00:18:59.773 --> 00:19:00.333
And indeed,

00:19:00.774 --> 00:19:03.075
The workers call it the Stadium of Miracles.

00:19:04.355 --> 00:19:07.859
Because we encountered difficulties in building this stadium in less than two years.

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:12.562
It was necessary to demolish and build a new stadium.

00:19:13.563 --> 00:19:14.702
And it was a true miracle.

00:19:16.884 --> 00:19:19.787
The lack of space and the narrowness of the construction site were a problem.

00:19:20.386 --> 00:19:22.669
There were 50 cranes on the construction site at the same time.

00:19:22.848 --> 00:19:26.332
50 cranes that had to be moved to transport the equipment.

00:19:26.811 --> 00:19:28.413
and assemble this enormous construction set.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:37.567
But to facilitate this colossal undertaking and build the stadium in less than 24 months,

00:19:38.229 --> 00:19:40.392
The roof is detached from the rest of the building.

00:19:43.477 --> 00:19:46.740
The Italian National Olympic Committee is designing the project.

00:19:49.605 --> 00:19:52.009
The roof structure must cover all the stands.

00:19:52.568 --> 00:19:54.752
but so as not to obstruct the spectators' view,

00:19:55.273 --> 00:19:59.019
It is necessary to avoid using a load-bearing structure inside the stadium.

00:20:01.401 --> 00:20:11.730
The weight of the roof is then supported by a whole structure of beams and cables located above the roof and supported by 8 gigantic columns at the 4 corners of the stadium.

00:20:16.663 --> 00:20:25.407
The reinforced concrete towers can reach over 70 meters in height and the main roof structure is between 45 and 55 meters high.

00:20:27.307 --> 00:20:31.127
The entire roof structure represents more than a third of the size of the stadium.

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:39.411
Constrained by time,

00:20:39.971 --> 00:20:41.932
The task facing the builders is immense.

00:20:43.172 --> 00:20:45.274
Especially since an unexpected event is about to occur.

00:20:46.155 --> 00:20:47.816
One month after the start of the work,

00:20:48.356 --> 00:20:49.477
The project is suspended.

00:20:55.002 --> 00:21:01.287
This imposing roof is rejected by the Ministry of Cultural Heritage and the Environment and by the Administrative Court of Rome.

00:21:03.008 --> 00:21:06.691
The eight towers, each over 50 meters tall, have too great an impact on the landscape.

00:21:11.055 --> 00:21:11.916
For manufacturers...

00:21:12.475 --> 00:21:13.817
It's a real blow.

00:21:15.538 --> 00:21:21.900
We have to start all over again from scratch.

00:21:22.581 --> 00:21:26.344
We found ourselves with a blank page 16 months before the inauguration.

00:21:28.865 --> 00:21:30.785
The height of the columns was the main problem.

00:21:30.965 --> 00:21:33.907
We needed to find the lowest possible solution.

00:21:36.729 --> 00:21:37.589
Everything had to be redone.

00:21:37.789 --> 00:21:39.250
the project and the entire construction.

00:21:46.104 --> 00:21:47.505
The challenge was already immense.

00:21:48.146 --> 00:21:53.230
But now it is a real feat that architects and engineers must accomplish hand in hand.

00:21:57.994 --> 00:22:01.257
This roof needs to be as low as possible and quick to build.

00:22:05.161 --> 00:22:09.004
It was ultimately the architect Massimo Maggiovichi who found the solution.

00:22:11.486 --> 00:22:13.528
Build a roof using a bicycle wheel.

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:20.871
That's when I came up with this new idea.

00:22:21.811 --> 00:22:24.252
which had never been achieved in such a large stadium.

00:22:27.014 --> 00:22:31.297
That is to say, the idea of ​​a bicycle wheel that is completely independent of the rest.

00:22:34.259 --> 00:22:39.382
It doesn't need to be supported by large structures like these tall towers.

00:22:40.021 --> 00:22:40.301
Actually,

00:22:40.382 --> 00:22:41.202
Everything is contained within this ring.

00:22:41.462 --> 00:22:42.983
which can actually be very low.

00:22:44.365 --> 00:22:46.266
Because this structural concept allows it.

00:22:50.709 --> 00:22:51.870
This revolutionary idea,

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:53.911
first conceived in a stadium,

00:22:54.291 --> 00:22:56.032
is immediately validated by the authorities.

00:23:00.515 --> 00:23:02.517
The roof structure resembles a bicycle wheel.

00:23:04.077 --> 00:23:05.198
The center of the roof,

00:23:05.659 --> 00:23:06.519
the inner ring,

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:10.382
is made up of 12 steel cables almost 9 cm in diameter.

00:23:11.503 --> 00:23:13.183
They represent the center of the bicycle wheel.

00:23:18.468 --> 00:23:21.049
80 junctions help to reinforce the inner ring.

00:23:23.732 --> 00:23:28.956
From these junctions extend the steel cable lattices which are comparable to the radius of the bicycle road.

00:23:31.138 --> 00:23:34.421
Each lattice consists of a top cable and a bottom cable.

00:23:36.562 --> 00:23:41.047
They are connected to each other by vertical cables for added stability and support.

00:23:44.861 --> 00:23:48.122
Each trellis is attached to what could be considered the rim.

00:23:48.982 --> 00:23:50.982
a peripheral anchoring structure.

00:23:55.025 --> 00:23:58.846
This structure is made up of steel tubes about twelve meters high.

00:24:00.628 --> 00:24:05.088
The entire structure is connected to the outer ring, which is supported by 16 columns which,

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:06.190
to support the weight,

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:08.651
must be extremely robust.

00:24:14.339 --> 00:24:17.221
To minimize the weight supported by these 16 columns,

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:19.461
The choice of membrane is crucial.

00:24:22.423 --> 00:24:23.582
The ideal combination?

00:24:24.682 --> 00:24:27.844
A fiberglass layer that forms the resistant part of the membrane,

00:24:28.585 --> 00:24:31.625
covered with a polytetrafluoroethylene film,

00:24:32.165 --> 00:24:37.067
a type of plastic that guarantees the impermeability and protection of the fiberglass.

00:24:41.515 --> 00:24:43.958
The engineers have accomplished a remarkable feat.

00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:46.822
To create a sophisticated roof,

00:24:47.283 --> 00:24:49.666
light and low in less than 16 months.

00:24:55.114 --> 00:24:59.019
This race against time earned it the nickname Stadium of Miracles.

00:25:04.481 --> 00:25:04.903
Today,

00:25:05.022 --> 00:25:05.823
30 years later,

00:25:08.365 --> 00:25:16.989
I wonder how I found the courage to propose this solution, which had never been implemented before.

00:25:17.710 --> 00:25:18.930
I must admit that at that moment,

00:25:18.990 --> 00:25:23.413
We lacked the knowledge to guarantee a perfect result.

00:25:25.973 --> 00:25:26.294
Actually,

00:25:26.354 --> 00:25:27.755
We trusted our intuition.

00:25:28.295 --> 00:25:29.135
But as we know,

00:25:29.791 --> 00:25:31.952
We must always push the boundaries of technology.

00:25:35.595 --> 00:25:43.619
It is therefore the imagination and audacity of this man that made it possible to achieve this architectural feat and to make this roof a global reference.

00:25:59.243 --> 00:26:01.246
The other major innovation of the Olympic stadium,

00:26:01.985 --> 00:26:03.887
It's an extension of the TV stand.

00:26:05.288 --> 00:26:06.590
It owes its name to the river.

00:26:06.810 --> 00:26:07.310
the Tiber,

00:26:07.811 --> 00:26:10.433
which crosses Rome and passes close to the city walls.

00:26:13.797 --> 00:26:16.179
During the massive construction work of 1990,

00:26:17.079 --> 00:26:20.603
The TV stand is the only part of the stadium that has been preserved.

00:26:24.432 --> 00:26:25.515
The rest of the enclosure,

00:26:25.634 --> 00:26:28.020
constructed primarily with low-quality cement,

00:26:28.582 --> 00:26:29.924
was completely destroyed.

00:26:54.173 --> 00:26:59.436
The Tévéré stand was left and reinforced because it is a testament to the old stadium.

00:27:02.358 --> 00:27:05.780
The walls between Avertin and the fountains can still be seen.

00:27:08.363 --> 00:27:10.625
Travertine was used as a symbol.

00:27:12.906 --> 00:27:18.850
We left it as is and just enlarged the upper wooden section.

00:27:19.110 --> 00:27:19.411
Like that,

00:27:19.932 --> 00:27:24.375
We can still admire the symbols of the continuity of the stadium's history.

00:27:27.677 --> 00:27:27.937
SO,

00:27:28.218 --> 00:27:29.499
even if we redid everything,

00:27:30.279 --> 00:27:35.302
We have thus preserved a historical record of the TV stand.

00:27:37.644 --> 00:27:44.212
The Tévéré stand was therefore extended by 16 additional rows to accommodate the 70,000 spectators in the stadium.

00:27:47.878 --> 00:27:54.566
The engineers therefore had to innovate to increase the height of the grandstand while minimizing the weight borne by the existing structure.

00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:02.681
Jaime Manca,

00:28:03.260 --> 00:28:05.482
architect and specialist in wooden stadiums,

00:28:06.124 --> 00:28:07.585
takes us to the foot of the grandstand.

00:28:12.009 --> 00:28:13.310
Here is the Tevere stand,

00:28:14.010 --> 00:28:17.093
produced in 1990 for the World Cup.

00:28:20.037 --> 00:28:22.480
Above this reinforced concrete pillar structure,

00:28:23.240 --> 00:28:25.845
We created a structure using laminated wood.

00:28:27.046 --> 00:28:31.972
This lightweight structure supports inclined beams which in turn support the aluminium bleachers.

00:28:33.094 --> 00:28:35.817
All of this makes it possible to have an ultra-lightweight system.

00:28:47.696 --> 00:28:50.598
It is a material that weighs 500 kg per cubic meter.

00:28:50.858 --> 00:28:53.821
It is therefore significantly lighter than any other material.

00:28:54.642 --> 00:28:55.302
Reinforced concrete,

00:28:55.402 --> 00:28:55.562
him,

00:28:55.662 --> 00:28:57.625
weighs 2500 kg per cubic meter.

00:28:58.024 --> 00:28:58.425
Steel,

00:28:58.465 --> 00:29:00.767
more than 6000.

00:29:01.247 --> 00:29:04.990
Its extreme lightness makes it a very easy material to use.

00:29:06.441 --> 00:29:10.746
It allows for a very simple site setup and quick assembly.

00:29:13.269 --> 00:29:15.211
We fit together parallel epipedals,

00:29:15.471 --> 00:29:17.235
It's a bit like assembling a giant Lego set.

00:29:28.983 --> 00:29:35.145
Laminated wood is made by assembling boards coated with melamine glue and pressed together.

00:29:41.608 --> 00:29:41.868
So,

00:29:42.288 --> 00:29:43.009
after 12 hours,

00:29:43.528 --> 00:29:45.809
This results in a beam known as a gloulam beam.

00:29:58.709 --> 00:30:00.000
These wooden beams and these wood seeds are wooden beams.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:03.882
The aluminum cheapskates are the symbol of the expansion of the TV-style grandstand.

00:30:09.163 --> 00:30:11.444
But doesn't wood present a major risk?

00:30:12.306 --> 00:30:15.047
That of catching fire and bursting into flames very quickly.

00:30:19.949 --> 00:30:22.589
Glulam is flammable because it is a wood-based material.

00:30:23.230 --> 00:30:25.391
but it is a wood that catches fire very slowly.

00:30:27.900 --> 00:30:31.981
It reduces its carbon layer by 6 tenths of a millimeter per minute.

00:30:34.102 --> 00:30:37.323
Knowing this allows for predefined evacuation delay times.

00:30:37.743 --> 00:30:40.463
which would be impossible if other materials were used.

00:30:43.625 --> 00:30:44.345
For example,

00:30:44.566 --> 00:30:46.026
in case of high temperature,

00:30:46.266 --> 00:30:47.767
Steel has a tendency to collapse.

00:30:48.247 --> 00:30:49.126
At 800 degrees,

00:30:49.366 --> 00:30:52.188
It loses all its mechanical characteristics and collapses.

00:30:52.787 --> 00:30:57.710
Firefighters are therefore more likely to authorize a building made of gloulam rather than steel or reinforced concrete.

00:31:05.715 --> 00:31:06.835
Using gloulam,

00:31:07.576 --> 00:31:10.378
Rome's Olympic Stadium delivered a great performance.

00:31:11.778 --> 00:31:15.621
To build a new, extremely lightweight grandstand on top of an existing structure,

00:31:16.021 --> 00:31:16.301
and this,

00:31:16.781 --> 00:31:18.423
in record construction time.

00:31:26.115 --> 00:31:30.678
Stadium builders continue to demonstrate inventiveness and push their limits.

00:31:31.558 --> 00:31:33.339
This was the case of Massimo Maggiovichi,

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:36.980
who created the bicycle wheel roof for the Olympic Stadium in Rome.

00:31:44.605 --> 00:31:48.507
A revolutionary concept that gives it this very distinctive appearance.

00:31:59.083 --> 00:32:00.183
But in the Basque city,

00:32:00.843 --> 00:32:04.204
The architect of the San Mames stadium had to face a new challenge.

00:32:07.086 --> 00:32:07.905
At the end of the work,

00:32:08.466 --> 00:32:11.506
The enclosure is covered by a roof that protects the stands from the rain.

00:32:15.908 --> 00:32:20.269
But the city is subject to regular bad weather and after a few months of use,

00:32:21.689 --> 00:32:27.331
Athletic Bilbao finds that the roof of the new stadium does not adequately protect the pitch and the lower part of the stands.

00:32:30.347 --> 00:32:32.789
Architects are then faced with a new challenge.

00:32:34.010 --> 00:32:37.953
Carrying out a roof extension while the construction work is finished.

00:32:46.339 --> 00:32:50.903
It was a really big engineering challenge because there is nothing similar in the world.

00:32:52.584 --> 00:32:57.488
A 50-meter-long metal structure that supports an extension

00:32:58.167 --> 00:32:58.288
Who,

00:32:58.407 --> 00:32:58.587
they,

00:32:58.607 --> 00:33:01.448
They measure between 18 and 23 meters in length, depending on the area.

00:33:02.769 --> 00:33:04.669
and all held together by taut cables.

00:33:07.911 --> 00:33:09.111
The existing cover,

00:33:09.511 --> 00:33:11.232
with a cantilever of 50 meters,

00:33:11.832 --> 00:33:14.373
It was not designed to support additional weight.

00:33:16.334 --> 00:33:18.714
The extension must therefore be as lightweight as possible.

00:33:23.298 --> 00:33:26.340
The architects immediately considered the most suitable solution,

00:33:27.621 --> 00:33:28.643
the roof made of a bicycle wheel.

00:33:34.907 --> 00:33:35.307
First of all,

00:33:35.528 --> 00:33:39.590
a new steel tube structure is fixed to the edge of the old structure.

00:33:40.751 --> 00:33:47.395
It allows for the accommodation of a system of cables stretched between tubes which together form a complete oval-shaped structure.

00:33:55.019 --> 00:34:00.383
On top of this are positioned inclined metal frames onto which plastic film is placed.

00:34:03.647 --> 00:34:09.932
The whole thing is then inflated and allows rainwater to be collected at the junction between the two parts of the roof.

00:34:12.195 --> 00:34:12.695
In the end,

00:34:13.516 --> 00:34:19.501
The extension is 14.92 m at the shortest width and up to 23 m in the curves.

00:34:23.505 --> 00:34:26.867
We worked to create a very lightweight cover.

00:34:27.168 --> 00:34:32.052
simply made from steel cables connected to the existing roof using reinforcements.

00:34:33.525 --> 00:34:34.026
Together,

00:34:34.346 --> 00:34:37.629
They form a structure commonly referred to as the bicycle wheel system.

00:34:39.391 --> 00:34:45.537
This extension is therefore designed as if it were a bicycle wheel, with the cables representing the spokes of the wheel.

00:34:46.177 --> 00:34:51.643
We were able to give it this shape and integrate it harmoniously into the architecture of the rest of the stadium.

00:34:56.405 --> 00:34:57.386
To make matters worse,

00:34:58.427 --> 00:35:01.650
The bicycle wheel roof structure functions as a single unit.

00:35:02.090 --> 00:35:04.312
which requires extremely meticulous installation.

00:35:08.836 --> 00:35:11.839
Especially since the work had to be completed in less than 4 months.

00:35:12.319 --> 00:35:13.740
during the summer league break.

00:35:36.030 --> 00:35:37.391
To achieve this feat,

00:35:38.032 --> 00:35:41.654
The architects used an extremely lightweight roofing material.

00:35:42.334 --> 00:35:42.875
Ethylene,

00:35:43.135 --> 00:35:44.456
tetrafluoroethylene

00:35:45.056 --> 00:35:45.916
said ETFE.

00:35:49.897 --> 00:35:52.499
Philippe Lennert is the head of Vector Foil Tech,

00:35:53.039 --> 00:35:56.821
the only company in the world to have made ETFs its core business.

00:36:03.265 --> 00:36:09.829
He reveals to us the manufacturing secrets of this material used in the greatest contemporary architectural projects.

00:36:13.694 --> 00:36:15.155
In this part of the design office,

00:36:15.695 --> 00:36:21.059
We define all the information intended for the production of the TFE panels.

00:36:21.219 --> 00:36:26.582
So all the people you see here are working on the smallest details of the design of the TFE panels.

00:36:26.842 --> 00:36:27.403
For example...

00:36:27.823 --> 00:36:29.104
How to cut the leaves?

00:36:29.444 --> 00:36:30.665
How do I weld them together?

00:36:31.886 --> 00:36:33.327
This is where it all begins.

00:36:34.408 --> 00:36:41.612
They are then transferred to production where we weld together the different sheets of TFE to obtain a complete panel.

00:36:47.777 --> 00:36:49.978
The TFE is composed of resin,

00:36:50.558 --> 00:36:53.861
small granules that are melted and then transformed into a flexible film.

00:36:57.609 --> 00:36:59.391
When the designers have finished their project,

00:37:00.091 --> 00:37:02.673
The workshop takes over and carries out the first step,

00:37:03.254 --> 00:37:04.295
cutting the material.

00:37:09.619 --> 00:37:15.424
It is on these large automated tables that the ETF film is carefully cut into the desired shapes.

00:37:23.669 --> 00:37:28.040
The second production step consists of welding the TFE sheets together.

00:37:35.767 --> 00:37:36.007
Here,

00:37:36.267 --> 00:37:42.554
The single sheets of TFE that we cut from the roll are assembled and welded into a continuous layer.

00:37:44.776 --> 00:37:46.117
And then on these large tables,

00:37:46.177 --> 00:37:49.721
The layers are placed one on top of the other to create the TFE cushions.

00:37:54.013 --> 00:37:58.134
While Vector Foil Tech has complete mastery of the ETF production chain,

00:37:59.154 --> 00:38:00.254
each new major project,

00:38:00.614 --> 00:38:01.595
like that of a stadium,

00:38:02.115 --> 00:38:03.835
constitutes a real challenge.

00:38:08.636 --> 00:38:11.317
Stadium projects are generally our biggest projects.

00:38:12.557 --> 00:38:16.938
The whole process can really take a lot of time and use a lot of manpower.

00:38:18.638 --> 00:38:19.578
In many cases,

00:38:20.159 --> 00:38:22.019
We work 24 hours a day.

00:38:22.259 --> 00:38:23.060
7 days a week,

00:38:24.181 --> 00:38:28.125
with 3 teams to create a 20,000-seat stadium,

00:38:28.185 --> 00:38:30.166
30,000 or 40,000 m2,

00:38:30.527 --> 00:38:33.269
which represents a huge amount of manufacturing.

00:38:37.393 --> 00:38:39.835
Such was the challenge for the roof of the San Manes stadium.

00:38:40.296 --> 00:38:43.519
which is made up of 20,000 m2 of inflatable plastic cushions.

00:38:49.665 --> 00:38:50.747
The facade of the enclosure,

00:38:50.928 --> 00:38:52.391
also composed of ETFE,

00:38:53.052 --> 00:38:55.096
is equipped with a lighting system which,

00:38:55.116 --> 00:38:55.898
on match nights,

00:38:56.399 --> 00:38:58.043
gives the stadium its full splendor.

00:39:13.937 --> 00:39:14.338
Today,

00:39:14.918 --> 00:39:18.522
If this material is used in the world's largest architectural projects,

00:39:19.062 --> 00:39:21.025
That's because it offers many advantages.

00:39:26.410 --> 00:39:29.193
The major advantage of ETFE compared to glass,

00:39:30.134 --> 00:39:30.875
It's lightness.

00:39:32.476 --> 00:39:32.977
For example,

00:39:33.698 --> 00:39:34.678
A final year project panel

00:39:35.679 --> 00:39:36.540
It's 1 to 5%

00:39:37.060 --> 00:39:38.381
the weight of a glass panel,

00:39:39.262 --> 00:39:42.504
which represents a significant saving in the coating material.

00:39:43.165 --> 00:39:47.248
And that also means you don't need such a large framework.

00:39:52.452 --> 00:39:54.293
What's interesting about the TFE,

00:39:54.874 --> 00:39:56.715
It's because it's the chemical counterpart of Teflon.

00:39:57.236 --> 00:39:58.857
that you may know with the frying pan.

00:40:00.454 --> 00:40:02.476
And it has a very important characteristic,

00:40:03.157 --> 00:40:05.058
the non-stick characteristic.

00:40:07.681 --> 00:40:08.522
With the TFE,

00:40:09.503 --> 00:40:13.626
This means that dirt doesn't really stick to the outside of the panels.

00:40:15.848 --> 00:40:19.912
Our clients don't have to spend a lot of time or money on exterior cleaning,

00:40:20.633 --> 00:40:22.294
because the rain takes care of it for them.

00:40:26.881 --> 00:40:27.682
UV resistant,

00:40:28.463 --> 00:40:30.424
It does not discolor or degrade.

00:40:34.808 --> 00:40:35.549
Translucent,

00:40:35.889 --> 00:40:39.812
It lets through a large amount of light which naturally nourishes the grass.

00:40:48.079 --> 00:40:49.300
So with ETFE,

00:40:49.841 --> 00:40:54.325
You are building a transparent or translucent building envelope for the long term.

00:40:55.045 --> 00:40:59.189
And not just something that will last 10 or 15 years and then need to be replaced.

00:41:07.237 --> 00:41:08.598
If within the San Mames stadium,

00:41:08.798 --> 00:41:10.119
We only play football.

00:41:14.704 --> 00:41:15.945
the Olympic Stadium in Rome,

00:41:16.225 --> 00:41:16.365
him,

00:41:17.006 --> 00:41:18.667
It accommodates many other disciplines.

00:41:24.033 --> 00:41:24.533
In total,

00:41:24.933 --> 00:41:28.875
More than 60 sporting events take place on the pitch each year.

00:41:29.595 --> 00:41:31.216
Lawns are under increasing strain.

00:41:32.116 --> 00:41:34.117
which therefore needs to be ever more resilient.

00:41:36.858 --> 00:41:37.778
Francesco Rossini,

00:41:38.018 --> 00:41:38.919
agricultural engineer,

00:41:39.319 --> 00:41:40.939
specialist in sports turf,

00:41:41.419 --> 00:41:43.180
works at the University of Viterbo.

00:41:48.430 --> 00:41:49.331
Depending on the sport,

00:41:49.831 --> 00:41:54.755
Each type of grass has technical specifications that must be respected for the game to be perfect.

00:41:58.777 --> 00:41:59.118
SO,

00:41:59.398 --> 00:42:00.298
THE...

00:42:01.299 --> 00:42:11.023
The characteristics of a stadium pitch must be different from those of a golf course or polo field or even a tennis pitch.

00:42:13.303 --> 00:42:16.985
Each sport has its specific characteristics that the pitch must respect.

00:42:19.706 --> 00:42:22.407
And in order for Rome's grass to withstand such activity,

00:42:23.247 --> 00:42:27.389
Francesco conducted laboratory tests to find the best formula.

00:42:31.534 --> 00:42:35.457
We focused on optimizing the turf at the Olympic stadium.

00:42:37.939 --> 00:42:43.843
And we found solutions so that it could be used for both football and rugby.

00:42:46.705 --> 00:42:49.086
And that's thanks to our recent research.

00:42:54.097 --> 00:42:56.739
While most stadiums use artificial turf,

00:42:57.540 --> 00:42:58.221
that of Rome,

00:42:58.421 --> 00:42:58.561
him,

00:42:59.021 --> 00:43:02.664
opted for a natural lawn capable of withstanding impacts,

00:43:03.365 --> 00:43:04.906
but also to the Mediterranean climate.

00:43:13.113 --> 00:43:17.537
A custom-designed lawn that combines two complementary grass species,

00:43:18.178 --> 00:43:21.120
the fat bermuda shorts and the English ryegrass.

00:43:31.132 --> 00:43:33.554
This combination of cultures designed in the United States,

00:43:33.894 --> 00:43:35.155
in Florida and California,

00:43:35.635 --> 00:43:37.957
It was adopted for our Mediterranean climate.

00:43:38.497 --> 00:43:40.258
in order to make the ground more resistant.

00:43:46.720 --> 00:43:47.120
Indeed,

00:43:47.200 --> 00:43:48.921
if we didn't have this type of lawn,

00:43:50.241 --> 00:43:58.143
we would not be able to host the 64 to 67 events that take place on average each year in the stadium.

00:43:58.343 --> 00:44:05.705
This composition provides all the necessary characteristics of torsional strength and soil hardness.

00:44:10.579 --> 00:44:14.762
It meets UEFA's criteria and as you can see,

00:44:15.323 --> 00:44:17.264
The root ball is extremely robust.

00:44:17.585 --> 00:44:23.089
but just enough so that football and rugby players can play there safely.

00:44:28.674 --> 00:44:31.456
With this system composed solely of natural species,

00:44:33.641 --> 00:44:37.120
We guarantee the same services and performance as a synthetic lawn.

00:44:42.742 --> 00:44:47.884
The thick bermuda shorts withstand high temperatures and create the solid mesh of the grassy carpet.

00:44:49.424 --> 00:44:51.485
With its density and ultra-fast growth,

00:44:52.085 --> 00:44:54.386
It is the most popular type of turf for sports fields.

00:44:56.266 --> 00:44:58.587
The second type of grass is perennial ryegrass.

00:44:59.747 --> 00:45:02.608
It is cold-resistant and withstands foot traffic very well.

00:45:03.928 --> 00:45:05.989
These seeds are sown on the grassy bermuda shorts,

00:45:06.489 --> 00:45:07.169
then covered.

00:45:07.169 --> 00:45:07.813
covered with earth,

00:45:08.095 --> 00:45:09.323
compacted and watered.

00:45:10.969 --> 00:45:13.251
The grass mat is 4 cm thick.

00:45:15.332 --> 00:45:18.473
It rests on a 4 cm layer of silica sand.

00:45:20.194 --> 00:45:22.856
Sand is composed of more than 180 different minerals.

00:45:24.096 --> 00:45:26.578
It dries very quickly and ensures water drainage.

00:45:26.958 --> 00:45:28.439
which maintains the quality of the grass.

00:45:29.779 --> 00:45:33.662
Beneath the sand is a 15 cm layer of volcanic soil.

00:45:34.822 --> 00:45:36.723
These small pebbles have many beneficial properties.

00:45:37.584 --> 00:45:39.145
It facilitates drainage.

00:45:40.065 --> 00:45:41.806
help reduce weed growth,

00:45:42.647 --> 00:45:46.690
They protect the roots from frost in winter and retain freshness in summer.

00:45:48.871 --> 00:45:51.253
All of this rests on one meter of soil.

00:45:58.357 --> 00:46:03.981
While the collaboration between the University of Viterbo and the Olympic Stadium has been a success in terms of the quality of the pitch,

00:46:05.162 --> 00:46:06.903
It also helps to protect the environment.

00:46:15.249 --> 00:46:17.470
We are trying to improve the quality of the turf,

00:46:19.552 --> 00:46:21.614
but also to protect the environment,

00:46:22.775 --> 00:46:29.060
by reducing the use of pesticides and fertilizers,

00:46:29.921 --> 00:46:34.344
and especially by optimizing the use of heating and lighting,

00:46:34.885 --> 00:46:36.606
which have a high energy cost.

00:46:39.909 --> 00:46:47.435
Rome's Olympic Stadium has gone to great lengths to ensure that its natural grass makes this arena one of the most beautiful playing venues on the planet.

00:46:56.162 --> 00:46:58.024
In the cathedral of football at San Mames,

00:46:58.785 --> 00:47:02.948
Football is a religion that transcends all generations and social classes.

00:47:05.917 --> 00:47:06.657
On match nights,

00:47:07.378 --> 00:47:09.719
The entire San Mames district is in turmoil.

00:47:17.462 --> 00:47:23.305
The supporters, in a procession, walk up the main avenue to the stadium before invading the esplanade.

00:47:28.245 --> 00:47:29.145
For manufacturers,

00:47:29.745 --> 00:47:32.726
It was essential to preserve this very special fervor,

00:47:33.207 --> 00:47:34.347
renowned throughout the world.

00:47:37.708 --> 00:47:41.929
This was the main challenge we had to overcome when designing the stadium.

00:47:42.830 --> 00:47:44.490
We needed to build a modern stadium.

00:47:44.510 --> 00:47:45.351
a larger stadium

00:47:45.731 --> 00:47:49.172
but we absolutely did not want to lose all the atmosphere that the old one had.

00:47:57.269 --> 00:47:57.809
The stadium,

00:47:58.009 --> 00:47:59.310
located in the heart of the city center,

00:47:59.871 --> 00:48:01.652
it had to occupy as little space as possible.

00:48:02.772 --> 00:48:03.493
And surprisingly,

00:48:03.973 --> 00:48:08.195
It is this factor that has allowed the mythical atmosphere of this cathedral of football to be preserved.

00:48:20.621 --> 00:48:21.722
To reduce its height,

00:48:22.463 --> 00:48:25.545
the stadium was initially buried 8 meters below the surface.

00:48:26.866 --> 00:48:27.327
The stands,

00:48:27.467 --> 00:48:27.587
them,

00:48:28.007 --> 00:48:29.649
were built as close as possible to the ground.

00:48:30.790 --> 00:48:31.330
And above all,

00:48:32.191 --> 00:48:36.815
They were tilted at the steepest angle permitted by international football authorities.

00:48:40.870 --> 00:48:43.372
To preserve the atmosphere of the old San Mamés,

00:48:44.112 --> 00:48:46.714
We also decided to slope the roof downwards.

00:48:47.154 --> 00:48:51.357
with all the beams of the metal structure pointing towards the center of the field.

00:48:54.659 --> 00:48:59.906
The acoustic pressure from the spectators therefore reverberates under the roof and travels onto the playing field.

00:49:03.230 --> 00:49:09.377
And the final factor that helps to achieve this atmosphere is to give homogeneity to all things.

00:49:09.377 --> 00:49:09.957
All the stands,

00:49:09.958 --> 00:49:10.798
to the entire audience,

00:49:11.419 --> 00:49:14.141
this red ambiance with all these seats,

00:49:14.601 --> 00:49:15.462
the white of the roof,

00:49:15.983 --> 00:49:17.164
the green of the lawn,

00:49:17.564 --> 00:49:21.788
All of this amplifies the unique atmosphere of football, which is experienced in a special way.

00:49:22.088 --> 00:49:24.750
as was the case in the old San Mames and now here.

00:49:28.373 --> 00:49:29.094
And on the ground,

00:49:29.834 --> 00:49:32.276
The players also feel this legendary atmosphere.

00:49:35.518 --> 00:49:40.219
I was fortunate enough to be the last captain of the old stadium and the first captain of the new one.

00:49:41.920 --> 00:49:43.000
In the old Saint-Mames,

00:49:43.260 --> 00:49:45.481
As soon as you climbed the steps and saw the field,

00:49:46.021 --> 00:49:47.142
It reeked of football.

00:49:47.362 --> 00:49:47.502
No ?

00:49:49.802 --> 00:49:50.163
NOW,

00:49:50.203 --> 00:49:50.703
in the new one,

00:49:51.323 --> 00:49:52.423
when everyone sings,

00:49:52.523 --> 00:49:53.644
Everyone stand up,

00:49:53.964 --> 00:49:56.545
when the team traps the opposing team in the penalty area...

00:49:57.841 --> 00:49:58.201
Oh dear,

00:49:58.361 --> 00:49:59.022
That's great!

00:50:01.263 --> 00:50:01.744
I mean,

00:50:02.284 --> 00:50:04.386
The atmosphere in the stadium is deafening.

00:50:07.287 --> 00:50:08.388
And the players notice it.

00:50:08.628 --> 00:50:10.510
because their hair stands on end.

00:50:11.070 --> 00:50:12.811
And it's one of the most beautiful moments I've ever experienced.

00:50:13.492 --> 00:50:26.541
The atmosphere is incredible.

00:50:27.545 --> 00:50:29.667
The stadium is much more symmetrical than the old one.

00:50:29.767 --> 00:50:32.168
It is much more compact and people are closer to the grass.

00:50:32.569 --> 00:50:33.049
With all that,

00:50:33.109 --> 00:50:34.570
The atmosphere at the matches is incredible.

00:50:47.499 --> 00:50:47.959
In Rome,

00:50:48.780 --> 00:50:55.065
The two clubs in the capital can also count on their supporters to make the arena vibrate and their chants resonate all the way to the Vatican.

00:50:58.153 --> 00:51:04.379
Rome's Olympic Stadium and Bilbao's San Mames Stadium have successfully achieved the incredible feat of reinventing themselves in record time.

00:51:04.799 --> 00:51:05.100
and this,

00:51:05.500 --> 00:51:07.382
using cutting-edge technologies.

00:51:10.845 --> 00:51:12.487
Having become veritable institutions,

00:51:13.107 --> 00:51:15.289
Their fame extends far beyond national borders.

00:51:15.890 --> 00:51:17.671
attracting viewers from all over the world.

